some notes about formatting so we can make a handbook to keep this organized:

1: for each class there will be a default unlocked skill called the [className]_root (for its id), which will have the nether star icon and provide the starting attributes for each class. this should not require any unlocking and should come with the class

2: there will be 3 branches from the root which all connect to 3 diiferent subclasses
2.1: prior to the subclass selection, there will be 7 tiers (skills) on each branch before the subclasses
2.2: each of the tiers on each branch will increase the branch specific attribute bonuses and penalties
2.3: the id for each tier will be [className]_[branchName]_[tier]
2.4: each branch should have 2-5 positive attributes and 0-2 negative attributes, which increase as commitment does ( i do not know how to scale the debuffs without nuking other branch benefits so i am considering dropping the idea)
2.5: example: the warrior class has 3 branches: offense, defense, and utility
    offense:
        i. attack speed
        ii. attack damage
        iii. crit damage
        iv. movement speed
        v. stamina
    defense:
        i. armor
        ii. regen
        iii. max health
        iv. block absorption
    utility:
        i. kill xp
        ii. attack range
        iii. mana regen

2.6: traits should also scale and be granted based on attributes. these formulas will be made and only used in the KubeJS scripts, and will be determined by stages, attributes, and nbt data. puffish_skills will not every see anything related to attributes, as by default, attributes and stage progression will increase or decrease traits

3. there needs to be a predefined icon for each skill type (tier, branch, class unlock, etc.)

4. the neegative attributes need to scale with the positive, increasing class specialization, but not increasing subclass specialization. All of the subclass specialization should be enforced positively, not negatively.

5. the subclass selction will provide a minor buff in the related attributes, have a specific icon specified in point 4, and will have the id structure: [className]_[subclassName]_unlock. It will also open the subclass_[subclassName] stage for GameStages

6. after the subclass has been seleted, there will be 4-5 abilities with more attribute buffs, totaling 7 skill 'nodes'
6.1: the subclass nodes will have the id structure: [className]_[subclass]_[tier] where tier resets back to 1 after the subclass unlock

7. mastery nodes come after all of a specific subclass' nodes have been unlocked.
7.1: when unlocked the gamestage [className]_[subclassName]_mastery stage will be opened by GameStages
7.2: instead of adding massive perks and attribute bonses, power skills (or things like skill buffs of previous skills) should be granted (instantly on unlock or gradually with more progression).

8: extra...
8.1: adding skills in a seperate tree for non-class related attribute increases (mining speed, consumption speed, hunger, etc. for a warrior) for Slice of life improvements without breaking the class gameplay lock would be premissible but it is not necessary

9. make a handbook with this information, but before you do, make sure this information provided is enough to do so. check with the user regarding your concerns.
